    {
      "id": "5851bdf3368a986d0cf295013aadadb2",
      "title": "Ministry of New and Renewable Energy Successfully Concludes Special Campaign 6",
      "url": "https://pib.gov.in/PressReleaseIframePage.aspx?PRID=2334368",
      "date": "2026-11-09",
      "scraped_date": "2026-11-09",
      "relative_time": "Yesterday",
      "region": "Delhi",
      "verticals": [
        "Environmental_Health"
      ],
      "primary_vertical": "Environmental_Health",
      "sub_verticals": [],
      "tier": "primary",
      "relevance_score": 10.5,
      "snippet": "",
      "full_content": "Special Campaign 6 focused on institutionalising Swachhata, improving office management and reducing pendency\nThe Ministry of New and Renewable Energy (MNRE) has successfully concluded the implementation phase of Special Campaign 6 for Disposal of Pending Matters (SCDPM 6). The campaign was undertaken from 2nd October to 31st October 2026.\nThe campaign focused on institutionalising Swachhata, improving office management and reducing pendency across the Ministry, its attached organisations, Autonomous Bodies and Public Sector Undertakings (PSUs).\nDuring the implementation phase, the Ministry undertook various activities aimed at improving cleanliness and workplace management. Special emphasis was placed on the identification, collection, segregation and disposal of electronic waste (e-waste), ensuring better utilisation of available office space and promoting environmentally responsible waste management practices.\nThe Ministry made concerted efforts towards achieving the targets set under the campaign, with maximum targets successfully accomplished across the identified areas. Regular reviews and inspections of office sections were also undertaken to assess cleanliness, proper maintenance of official spaces and progress in the disposal of files and other pending matters. Officers and staff actively participated in the campaign, contributing towards maintaining clean and organised workplaces and improving administrative efficiency.\nThe campaign also witnessed active participation from the Ministry’s Autonomous Bodies and PSUs, ensuring a coordinated approach towards achieving the objectives.\nWith the successful conclusion of the implementation phase, MNRE reiterates its commitment to sustaining the achievements of the campaign through regular cleanliness drives, efficient file management, responsible e-waste disposal and a culture of accountability and timely disposal of pending matters.",
      "summary": "Special Campaign 6 focused on institutionalising Swachhata, improving office management and reducing pendency The Ministry of New and Renewable Energy (MNRE) has successfully concluded the implementation phase of Special Campaign 6 for Disposal of Pending Matters (SCDPM 6). The campaign was undertaken from 2nd October to 31st October 2026. The campaign focused on institutionalising Swachhata, improving office management and reducing pendency across the Ministry, its attached organisations, Autonomous Bodies and Public Sector Undertakings (PSUs).",
      "sentiment": "neutral",
      "section": "vertical"
    },
